IMPORT prelude

-- Government Proceedings Act 1956 (Singapore) -- when the Government can be sued and for what (ss 4 to 7, 12, 14), who sues for
-- public nuisances and public trusts (ss 8, 9), the priority of Government debts (s 10), whom to name as defendant (s 19), transfer
-- to the High Court (s 25), the relief a court may give against the Government (s 27), when a successful claimant may ask for a
-- certificate of the order (s 31), and proceedings in rem against Government property (s 35).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GPA1956.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 8 of 2026 (wef 29 May 2026, s 7) and Act 25 of 2021 (wef 1 April 2022) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the questions a claimant against the
-- Government, or a debtor of it, actually meets. Not encoded: s 3 (the Government's own right to sue), ss 13, 15 (contribution;
-- prerogative certificates), ss 16 to 18, 20 to 24, 26, 28 (procedure, service, revenue summary applications, interpleader, suits
-- against deceased persons, legal officers' audience), ss 29, 30, 32 to 34 (costs, interest, enforcement by the Government,
-- attachment, discovery), ss 36 to 38 (statutory defences, Rules of Court, savings), and anything left to Rules of Court.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Government Proceedings Act 1956 -- claims against the Government`

§§ `4 -- claims other than in tort`

-- s 4: "any claim against the Government which -- (a) is founded on the use or occupation or the right to the use or occupation of
-- State land; (b) arises out of the revenue laws; (c) arises out of any contract made by the authority of the Government which would,
-- if such claim had arisen between private persons, afford ground for civil proceedings; or (d) is a claim (other than a claim in
-- tort) for damages or compensation not included in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) which might lawfully be enforced by civil proceedings
-- as between private persons, shall be enforceable by proceedings against the Government".
DECLARE `Non-tort claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim about State land`
    `a claim under the revenue laws`
    `a contract made by the authority of the Government`
    `a contract made without the Government's authority`
    `other damages or compensation`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Non-tort claim`, `it would ground civil proceedings between private persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is enforceable against the Government under s 4` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim about State land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim under the revenue laws` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contract made by the authority of the Government` THEN `it would ground civil proceedings between private persons`
    WHEN `a contract made without the Government's authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `other damages or compensation` THEN `it would ground civil proceedings between private persons`

§§ `5, 6 and 7 -- liability in tort and its limits`

-- s 5: the Government "shall be liable for any wrongful act done or any neglect or default committed by any public officer in the
-- same manner and to the same extent as ... a principal, being a private person, is liable for ... his agent"; an officer "acting or
-- purporting in good faith to be acting in pursuance of a duty imposed by law shall be deemed to be the agent" of the Government.
-- s 6(1): no proceedings "unless proceedings for damages ... would have lain against such officer personally".
-- s 6(3): none for anything done "while discharging or purporting to discharge any responsibilities of a judicial nature" or "in
-- connection with the execution of judicial process".
-- s 6(4): none unless the officer was "employed by the Government and paid ... wholly out of the revenues of the Government, or any
-- fund certified by the Minister responsible for finance", or held an office the Minister certifies would normally be so paid.
-- s 7(1): "Notwithstanding any other provisions of this Act to the contrary, no proceedings, other than proceedings for breach of
-- contract, shall lie against the Government on account of anything done or omitted to be done or refused to be done by the
-- Government or any public officer in exercise of the public duties of the Government."
-- s 7(3): "Nothing in this section shall prevent the bringing of any suit for damages or compensation arising out of negligence or
-- trespass in the execution of any works of construction or maintenance (including in the performance of coastal management)".
DECLARE `Tort claim` HAS
    `a private principal would be liable for the officer as agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer would be personally liable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was judicial or in executing judicial process` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer was paid wholly from Government revenues or a certified fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was in exercise of the public duties of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is negligence or trespass in executing construction or maintenance works` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 14 bars the claim` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Tort claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 bars the claim` IF
        `the claim`'s `the act was in exercise of the public duties of the Government`
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the claim is negligence or trespass in executing construction or maintenance works`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Tort claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government is liable in tort` IF
        `the claim`'s `a private principal would be liable for the officer as agent`
    AND `the claim`'s `the officer would be personally liable`
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `the act was judicial or in executing judicial process`)
    AND `the claim`'s `the officer was paid wholly from Government revenues or a certified fund`
    AND (NOT `s 7 bars the claim` `the claim`)
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `s 14 bars the claim`)

-- s 7(2): "exercise of the public duties" INCLUDES (a) railways, roads or bridges; (b) schools, hospitals or other public buildings;
-- (c) sewerage, drainage, flood prevention and reclamation works; (d) the channels of rivers and waterways; (e) "the performance of
-- coastal management" -- (c) to (e) as amended by Act 8 of 2026 wef 29/05/2026. The list is inclusive: an activity not named may
-- still be a public duty; this function says only whether s 7(2) names it.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `road, railway or bridge works`
    `school, hospital or public building works`
    `sewerage, drainage, flood prevention or reclamation works`
    `river or waterway channel works`
    `coastal management`
    `an activity s 7(2) does not name`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(2) names the activity as a public duty` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `an activity s 7(2) does not name` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `12 -- patents, trade marks and copyright`

-- s 12(1): where "after 25 February 1965, any employee or agent of the Government infringes a patent, a registered trade mark or any
-- copyright and the infringement is committed with the authority of the Government, civil proceedings ... shall ... lie against the
-- Government". (2): "Subject to this section, no proceedings shall lie" for such infringement. Dates are written as YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `infringed on` IS A NUMBER, `with the Government's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an infringement claim lies against the Government` IF
    `infringed on` > 19650225 AND `with the Government's authority`

§§ `14 -- members of the armed forces and police`

-- s 14(1): nothing done by a member of the forces "while on duty as such" subjects "either him or the Government to liability in
-- tort for causing the death of another person, or for causing personal injury" to another member, if (a) the victim was (i) on duty,
-- or (ii) not on duty but (A) on land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle used for the forces, or (B) on a journey to report for or
-- return home from duty; and (b) the Minister responsible for finance certifies that the harm "has been or will be treated as
-- attributable to service" for a disablement or death award. Proviso: the subsection "shall not exempt a member of the forces from
-- liability in tort" where the court is satisfied the act "was not connected with the execution of his duties".
-- s 14(5): "forces" includes the armed forces AND the police force (with volunteer, auxiliary and special police).
--
-- Reading: the proviso names only the member, so on its words the Government stays exempt even where the member does not. That is
-- how this is encoded; it is a reading of the text, not a decided point.
GIVEN `the wrongdoer was a forces member on duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the harm is death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was a forces member on duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was on forces land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was travelling to or from duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Finance Minister certifies the harm attributable to service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) exempts the Government` IF
        `the wrongdoer was a forces member on duty`
    AND `the harm is death or personal injury`
    AND (   `the victim was a forces member on duty`
         OR `the victim was on forces land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle`
         OR `the victim was travelling to or from duty`)
    AND `the Finance Minister certifies the harm attributable to service`

GIVEN `the wrongdoer was a forces member on duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the harm is death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was a forces member on duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was on forces land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the victim was travelling to or from duty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Finance Minister certifies the harm attributable to service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court is satisfied the act was unconnected with the wrongdoer's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) exempts the wrongdoer` IF
        `s 14(1) exempts the Government` `the wrongdoer was a forces member on duty` `the harm is death or personal injury` `the victim was a forces member on duty` `the victim was on forces land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle` `the victim was travelling to or from duty` `the Finance Minister certifies the harm attributable to service`
    AND (NOT `the court is satisfied the act was unconnected with the wrongdoer's duties`)

§ `Government Proceedings Act 1956 -- who sues, and the Government as creditor`

§§ `8 and 9 -- public nuisances and public trusts`

-- s 8(1): "In the case of a public nuisance the Attorney-General, or 2 or more persons having obtained the consent in writing of the
-- Attorney-General, may institute a suit, though no special damage has been caused". (2) other rights of suit are unaffected.
-- s 9(1): for a trust "for public, religious, social or charitable purposes", the Attorney-General "or 2 or more persons having an
-- interest in the trust and having obtained the consent in writing of the Attorney-General" may sue for the listed reliefs; (2) no
-- such suit "except in conformity with that subsection".
GIVEN `brought by the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of persons suing` IS A NUMBER, `with the AG's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sue for a public nuisance without special damage` IF
        `brought by the Attorney-General`
    OR (`number of persons suing` >= 2 AND `with the AG's written consent`)

GIVEN `brought by the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of persons suing` IS A NUMBER, `each has an interest in the trust` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with the AG's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sue for relief over a public or charitable trust` IF
        `brought by the Attorney-General`
    OR (`number of persons suing` >= 2 AND `each has an interest in the trust` AND `with the AG's written consent`)

§§ `10 -- priority of Government debts`

-- s 10(1): debts owed to the Government are entitled "from the date of the accrual thereof ... to a preference of payment over all
-- debts or claims of every kind which shall, subsequent to such date, have been contracted or incurred". (2): nothing affects a right
-- under "a mortgage or charge of immovable property duly registered". Dates are written as YYYYMMDD. A debt incurred on the same day
-- is not "subsequent" and so is not postponed.
GIVEN `Government debt accrued on` IS A NUMBER, `other debt incurred on` IS A NUMBER, `other debt is a registered mortgage of immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government debt is paid first` IF
        `other debt incurred on` > `Government debt accrued on`
    AND (NOT `other debt is a registered mortgage of immovable property`)

-- s 11: sureties for persons owing money to the Government "may be sued as principals".

§ `Government Proceedings Act 1956 -- suing the Government`

§§ `19 -- whom to name as defendant`

-- s 19(3): proceedings "shall be instituted against the appropriate authorised Government department, or, if none of the authorised
-- Government departments is appropriate or the person instituting the proceedings has any reasonable doubt whether any and if so which
-- of those departments is appropriate, against the Attorney-General". The list of authorised departments is gazetted (s 19(1)).
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the appropriate authorised department`
    `the Attorney-General`

GIVEN `an authorised department is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claimant reasonably doubts which` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Defendant
DECIDE `the defendant to name` IS
    IF `an authorised department is appropriate` AND (NOT `the claimant reasonably doubts which`)
    THEN `the appropriate authorised department`
    ELSE `the Attorney-General`

§§ `25 -- transfer from a State Court to the High Court`

-- s 25(1): on the Government's application, "there is produced ... a certificate of the Attorney-General" that the case involves an
-- important question of law, may be decisive of other cases, or should be transferred in the public interest or for any other
-- reason, the General Division "shall order the proceedings to be transferred". (2): if removal "is likely to occasion substantial
-- additional expenses" to another party, the court "may refuse ... unless the Government enters into an undertaking" to pay them.
GIVEN `the Government applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the AG's certificate is produced` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `substantial additional expense to the other party is likely` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Government undertakes to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court must order the transfer` IF
        `the Government applies`
    AND `the AG's certificate is produced`
    AND (   (NOT `substantial additional expense to the other party is likely`)
         OR `the Government undertakes to pay it`)

§§ `27 -- relief against the Government`

-- s 27(1) proviso (a): where relief "might in proceedings between private persons be granted by way of injunction or specific
-- performance, the court shall not grant an injunction or make an order for specific performance, but may in lieu thereof make an
-- order declaratory of the rights of the parties"; (b) for "the recovery of land or other property the court shall not make an order
-- for the recovery of the land or the delivery of the property, but may in lieu thereof make an order declaring that the claimant is
-- entitled". (2): no injunction or order against an officer if the effect would be relief against the Government that could not be
-- obtained against the Government.
DECLARE Relief IS ONE OF
    `an injunction`
    `specific performance`
    `an order for recovery of land`
    `an order for delivery of property`
    `damages`
    `a declaration of rights`

GIVEN `the relief` IS A Relief
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant it against the Government` IF
    CONSIDER `the relief`
    WHEN `an injunction` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `specific performance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order for recovery of land` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order for delivery of property` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the relief` IS A Relief, `the effect would be relief against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant it against an officer` IF
        (NOT `the effect would be relief against the Government`)
    OR  `the court may grant it against the Government` `the relief`

§§ `31 -- certificate of an order against the Government`

-- s 31(1): the proper officer "shall, on an application ... at any time after the expiration of 21 days from the date of the order
-- or, in case the order provides for the payment of costs and the costs require to be assessed, at any time after the costs have been
-- assessed, whichever is the later, issue ... a certificate". (3): the Government "shall ... pay" the certified amount with interest;
-- the court may suspend payment pending appeal. (4): "no enforcement order or attachment or process in the nature thereof shall be
-- issued out of any court for enforcing payment by the Government".
--
-- Day counting is an inference: "21 days from the date of the order" is read as excluding the day of the order, so the 21 days have
-- expired once 22 or more days have passed. `days since the order` counts calendar days.
GIVEN `days since the order` IS A NUMBER, `costs require assessment` IS A BOOLEAN, `costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate may be applied for` IF
        `days since the order` > 21
    AND (   (NOT `costs require assessment`)
         OR `costs have been assessed`)

-- s 31(4): the certificate procedure replaces execution.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `execution may issue against the Government` IS FALSE

§§ `35 -- proceedings in rem`

-- s 35(1): nothing authorises "proceedings in rem in respect of any claim against the Government, or the arrest, detention or sale of
-- any ship or aircraft, or of any cargo or other property belonging to the Government". (2): if proceedings in rem were brought "in
-- the reasonable belief that the ship, aircraft, cargo or other property did not belong to the Government", the court MAY order them
-- treated as in personam against the Government or another proper person.
GIVEN `the property belongs to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property may be arrested` IF
    NOT `the property belongs to the Government`

GIVEN `the property belongs to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claimant reasonably believed it did not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may let the claim continue in personam` IF
    `the property belongs to the Government` AND `the claimant reasonably believed it did not`
